       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n**Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.** The maximum prescription dose of oral ibuprofen is generally 3,200 mg/day, so this order is double that limit. Even at the maximum, 800 mg four times daily would be a more typical regimen. The patient's normal kidney and liver function and 70 kg weight don't change that ceiling.\n\nEntering medication orders also normally requires a licensed prescriber who can take responsibility for the dose. Please route this to the medicine team or the ordering physician.\n\nIf the team intends a dose within the usual range, such as 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day) or a lower dose, they can enter it directly, or I can enter it if they confirm the dose and give me the prescriber's name for the order note. If the 1600 mg dose was intentional, the prescriber should review it before it goes in."
      }
